WEBVTT

00:05.330 --> 00:06.850
(The morning reception is over)

00:06.930 --> 00:09.520
I worked really hard this morning.

00:09.850 --> 00:10.980
As a reward,

00:11.060 --> 00:14.810
should I try the recently raved-about
stewed hamburger steak for lunch?

00:14.900 --> 00:17.020
Wait a minute!

00:17.480 --> 00:18.650
Yes!

00:18.730 --> 00:20.240
I made it just in time!

00:20.990 --> 00:23.030
No, you didn't, okay?

00:23.110 --> 00:25.370
I had an urgent quest to accept.

00:25.450 --> 00:26.950
That's why I rushed here.

00:27.330 --> 00:28.450
If it's you, Alina,

00:28.540 --> 00:30.950
it's fine if I'm a little late, right?

00:31.410 --> 00:32.620
Just die.

00:33.080 --> 00:34.080
That's true.

00:34.170 --> 00:37.170
It's not like I can't accept it.

00:37.540 --> 00:39.840
But he's clearly a deliberate offender,

00:39.920 --> 00:42.090
is it really necessary
to be so nice to him?

00:42.170 --> 00:44.640
Even if it means sacrificing
my extremely precious lunch break?

00:44.930 --> 00:45.930
Alina.

00:46.010 --> 00:47.930
I'm sorry, but I'm in a hurry

00:48.010 --> 00:50.470
because I want to go have lunch.

00:54.310 --> 00:55.650
All right.

00:55.730 --> 00:57.520
I can still handle your request.

00:58.150 --> 01:00.860
Please write down the quest
you'd like to take on.

01:02.280 --> 01:03.650
How dare you

01:04.570 --> 01:07.320
ruin my lunch break!

01:07.410 --> 01:09.450
He deserves to die!

01:09.830 --> 01:12.500
Why don't you just turn him down?

01:12.580 --> 01:13.960
If he complains,

01:14.040 --> 01:16.130
wouldn't I have more work to do?

01:16.210 --> 01:17.380
And...

01:17.460 --> 01:18.500
And?

01:20.960 --> 01:22.170
All of this...

01:22.260 --> 01:24.090
Yes, all of this

01:25.260 --> 01:27.340
is for the Centennial Festival!

01:27.890 --> 01:29.890
The festival lasts for three days.

01:29.970 --> 01:33.350
But I was too busy working overtime
the past two years to make it.

01:33.640 --> 01:34.770
So this year,

01:34.850 --> 01:35.980
no matter what,

01:36.060 --> 01:38.360
I'll clock out on time!

01:38.650 --> 01:40.980
Are we going to be that busy?

01:41.070 --> 01:43.110
That's not the only thing.

01:43.940 --> 01:45.700
This place will become a battlefield.

01:47.110 --> 01:48.030
Why, you ask?

01:48.120 --> 01:50.120
It's because the quests accepted
during the Centennial Festival

01:50.200 --> 01:53.750
will offer more clear rewards than usual.

01:54.370 --> 01:56.580
Because it's the special bonus period.

01:57.540 --> 01:58.790
What the heck is that?

01:59.040 --> 02:01.960
When that happens,
the adventurers who are ready to go

02:02.050 --> 02:04.210
will flock to our counters.

02:04.300 --> 02:06.930
You know clearly
what will happen then, don't you?

02:07.800 --> 02:09.220
Death.

02:11.260 --> 02:12.350
Look at this!

02:12.890 --> 02:14.350
This is...

02:14.430 --> 02:16.770
This is based on
my two years of experience

02:16.850 --> 02:19.440
and outlines the trends
and countermeasures for the quest rush.

02:19.520 --> 02:20.440
And also!

02:21.400 --> 02:22.320
This is

02:22.400 --> 02:25.570
the schedule and guide
for the Centennial Festival.

02:25.820 --> 02:28.570
On the first and second days,
I'll eat while walking.

02:28.660 --> 02:30.280
On the third day is the main event,

02:30.370 --> 02:31.450
the Souls Rest Ceremony.

02:31.530 --> 02:32.740
All that's left to do

02:32.830 --> 02:35.450
is get off work on time on that day.

02:35.540 --> 02:36.620
That's amazing.

02:36.710 --> 02:38.540
All the bottled-up feelings

02:38.620 --> 02:40.670
have really ignited your motivation.

02:41.130 --> 02:42.920
Just wait for me, Centennial Festival!

02:43.000 --> 02:46.630
This year,
I'll definitely clock out on time!

02:48.050 --> 02:50.340
And then enjoy myself to the fullest!

02:54.850 --> 03:00.690
(I May Be a Guild Receptionist,
but I'll Solo Any Boss to Clock Out on Time)

04:21.100 --> 04:23.810
(Silver Sword Inn)

04:38.370 --> 04:43.460
Heave-ho...

04:46.380 --> 04:47.500
All right!

04:48.000 --> 04:50.510
This should do it.

04:57.760 --> 04:59.770
I'm not at my best yet.

05:01.680 --> 05:03.480
What are you doing?

05:03.560 --> 05:05.900
You can't move yet!

05:05.980 --> 05:07.860
This will reopen your wounds!

05:08.860 --> 05:10.980
But it doesn't hurt anymore,
so I should be fine.

05:11.240 --> 05:14.360
Your ribs broke
and pierced into your lungs.

05:14.740 --> 05:17.950
Please, just rest properly.

05:18.030 --> 05:20.410
I'm sorry. I get it.

05:20.490 --> 05:22.290
As long as you do.

05:22.620 --> 05:24.750
Here. This is for today.

05:25.540 --> 05:26.880
Why do I feel like

05:26.960 --> 05:28.590
it's gotten even worse?

05:28.670 --> 05:29.880
Don't worry.

05:29.960 --> 05:32.050
Jade already drank it.

05:41.430 --> 05:43.390
How was it? Did it work?

05:45.480 --> 05:47.060
Taste aside,

05:47.150 --> 05:48.480
I do feel more energetic.

05:48.560 --> 05:51.480
This is all I can do for you guys.

05:52.360 --> 05:54.740
Let me take care of you.

05:55.360 --> 05:57.320
I'm counting on you.

06:05.830 --> 06:09.130
It's so nice to get off work on time.

06:09.710 --> 06:12.250
The cake shop is still open.

06:12.670 --> 06:13.920
This is simply

06:14.010 --> 06:16.630
a privilege only the winner can enjoy.

06:21.720 --> 06:22.680
Let's see.

06:22.770 --> 06:24.850
I'll take this, this, and this.

06:24.930 --> 06:26.020
This too.

06:26.100 --> 06:27.480
Okay.

06:27.900 --> 06:30.900
Going on a cake-buying spree
on the way home from work

06:30.980 --> 06:35.240
is a luxury
only a working adult can enjoy!

06:35.570 --> 06:37.530
There's one strawberry tart left!

06:37.910 --> 06:39.870
- I'll also have a strawberry tart.
- One strawberry tart, please.

06:41.280 --> 06:42.370
- What?
- What?

06:55.420 --> 06:59.640
This is the taste
of getting off work on time.

07:01.180 --> 07:02.430
Well,

07:02.510 --> 07:06.810
I'm sorry for making you
give me the last one.

07:07.060 --> 07:08.440
It's fine.

07:08.520 --> 07:10.520
Savor this happiness.

07:10.600 --> 07:12.770
Don't worry about it.

07:13.770 --> 07:15.110
I'm sorry.

07:15.190 --> 07:18.070
I told you, you don't have
to apologize to me.

07:18.150 --> 07:20.410
Well...

07:20.740 --> 07:21.870
Then,

07:22.450 --> 07:24.030
I'm going to eat.

07:29.160 --> 07:30.580
I'm so happy.

07:30.670 --> 07:32.040
Right?

07:35.550 --> 07:38.970
Now I understand why Jade
is so infatuated with Ms. Alina.

07:42.550 --> 07:44.430
Do you come here often?

07:45.600 --> 07:47.020
Well, yes.

07:47.390 --> 07:51.270
After all, this place has
the best sweets in Ifuru.

07:51.350 --> 07:53.020
That's right!

07:53.310 --> 07:55.900
Lowe loves their grape jelly too.

07:55.980 --> 07:57.530
He's still recovering,

07:57.610 --> 07:59.280
so I wanted to buy one for him.

07:59.360 --> 08:00.650
As expected of a healer.

08:00.740 --> 08:02.320
You're so considerate of your companions.

08:02.410 --> 08:03.530
Well...

08:04.160 --> 08:05.830
I'm not that great.

08:06.870 --> 08:07.790
Back then,

08:07.870 --> 08:10.250
it was thanks to Ms. Alina's help.

08:10.330 --> 08:13.830
That's why Lowe, Jade, and I
are still alive.

08:14.460 --> 08:17.300
This is all thanks to you, Ms. Alina.

08:17.590 --> 08:18.630
Come on.

08:18.710 --> 08:20.470
Don't say things like that.

08:20.880 --> 08:22.970
Come on, let's eat.

08:24.930 --> 08:26.140
Okay.

08:37.440 --> 08:38.900
Ms. Alina!

08:39.820 --> 08:40.820
Hey.

08:40.900 --> 08:41.900
What do you want?

08:42.360 --> 08:45.490
Thank you for being friends with Lululi.

08:45.570 --> 08:46.410
You...

08:46.490 --> 08:48.080
Did you see everything?

08:48.160 --> 08:49.620
Let's not talk about that now.

08:49.700 --> 08:52.330
Actually, deep down inside,
I kind of believed in you.

08:52.710 --> 08:53.540
What for?

08:53.620 --> 08:57.000
That you would visit me at least once.

08:57.090 --> 09:00.590
Why do I have to go
all the way to see you?

09:00.670 --> 09:01.550
On top of that,

09:01.630 --> 09:04.090
you moved out of the inn right away.

09:04.180 --> 09:05.340
Now I feel lonely.

09:05.430 --> 09:07.550
My house is the most comfortable.

09:07.640 --> 09:10.720
I'm grateful that the Guild
is willing to pay for the repairs.

09:12.020 --> 09:14.650
But we're companions
who have faced life and death together.

09:14.730 --> 09:18.150
We just happened to be in the same spot
and fought together. That's all.

09:18.230 --> 09:20.230
Come on.

09:23.570 --> 09:24.610
I see.

09:24.700 --> 09:26.660
The Centennial Festival is coming up.

09:26.870 --> 09:29.740
I wish I could go
with everyone again this year.

09:38.130 --> 09:39.420
(10 Days Before the Centennial Festival)

09:39.500 --> 09:41.130
(10 Days Before the Centennial Festival)
All right!

09:41.210 --> 09:43.590
Let's work hard again today!

09:43.670 --> 09:46.260
You're all fired up, Ms. Alina.

09:46.340 --> 09:47.300
Of course.

09:47.390 --> 09:51.140
After all, the battle for the Centennial
Festival is just about to begin.

09:52.060 --> 09:54.060
That means

09:54.140 --> 09:55.770
you have a lover, right?

09:56.150 --> 09:57.310
A lover?

09:57.400 --> 09:59.860
You don't have to play dumb.

09:59.940 --> 10:01.530
Speaking of the Centennial Festival,

10:01.610 --> 10:05.030
isn't it a super, super
classic dating event?

10:05.740 --> 10:06.740
What's that?

10:07.200 --> 10:09.030
Wait a minute!

10:09.120 --> 10:10.410
If it's not a date,

10:10.490 --> 10:12.950
then who are you going with?

10:13.040 --> 10:13.950
I'm going alone.

10:14.040 --> 10:15.540
Alone?

10:15.870 --> 10:16.710
Why?

10:17.210 --> 10:21.590
Because there will be a lot of lovers
doing lovey-dovey stuff at the event.

10:21.670 --> 10:23.630
Are you planning to go there alone?

10:23.710 --> 10:25.630
Do you want to die?

10:25.720 --> 10:28.470
I just want to enjoy it by myself.
What's wrong with that?

10:28.550 --> 10:30.220
So strong!

10:30.300 --> 10:32.890
Is this the ultimate fate
of an overtime maniac?

10:32.970 --> 10:34.310
Hey!

10:35.680 --> 10:38.100
I'd love to go with you,

10:38.190 --> 10:41.440
but unfortunately,
I already have a date that day.

10:41.520 --> 10:42.610
I see.

10:43.070 --> 10:45.110
Aren't you curious who I'm going with?

10:45.190 --> 10:46.400
Not really.

10:48.070 --> 10:50.160
Don't be shocked, okay?

10:50.240 --> 10:52.160
He is...

10:53.120 --> 10:54.750
Lord Executioner!

10:55.790 --> 10:58.290
I hit a weird spot.

10:58.370 --> 11:01.460
Come on, you don't have
to be so surprised.

11:01.540 --> 11:03.630
A date with the Executioner?

11:03.710 --> 11:06.260
Could she have been deceived
by an impostor?

11:06.340 --> 11:09.130
You must think that's impossible, right?

11:09.220 --> 11:11.470
But it's indeed possible for me.

11:11.760 --> 11:12.930
All I have to do is

11:13.260 --> 11:16.020
to attend with the Lord Executioner doll.

11:18.230 --> 11:20.940
Even the details of this doll
are well-executed.

11:21.020 --> 11:22.310
And under this hood,

11:22.400 --> 11:25.940
the cool image of the Lord Executioner
I imagined has been recreated.

11:26.030 --> 11:27.820
Okay.

11:28.030 --> 11:29.450
It's almost time to open.

11:29.530 --> 11:31.280
Clean up quickly.

11:31.370 --> 11:32.530
What's the matter?

11:32.620 --> 11:34.870
Did you hear something?

11:39.080 --> 11:40.460
What is that?

11:40.540 --> 11:41.790
Open the door!

11:41.880 --> 11:42.710
I was here first!

11:42.790 --> 11:44.340
I'm counting on you!

11:46.670 --> 11:48.800
Wait...

11:49.550 --> 11:54.050
What's going on?

11:56.270 --> 11:58.850
It's finally done.

11:59.350 --> 12:02.100
What's with this amount?

12:02.190 --> 12:05.980
The special bonus period
hasn't started yet, right?

12:06.610 --> 12:08.530
How did this happen?

12:09.450 --> 12:10.950
Has something appeared

12:11.030 --> 12:13.200
that's very tempting for adventurers?

12:13.280 --> 12:14.580
Even so,

12:14.660 --> 12:16.660
no one knows what's going on.

12:17.040 --> 12:19.290
I don't want to use this method,

12:19.370 --> 12:21.500
but this isn't the time to say that.

12:21.870 --> 12:24.210
I'm going out for a while.

12:25.130 --> 12:27.130
Are you going to leave these and go home?

12:27.550 --> 12:29.550
Of course I'll be back.

12:29.630 --> 12:31.800
But I have to do something
about this abnormality first.

12:32.090 --> 12:34.390
I can't let this work drag on
until the Centennial Festival.

12:34.470 --> 12:35.680
That's the one thing

12:35.760 --> 12:39.140
I will never, ever let happen!

12:43.600 --> 12:44.440
Cybil!

12:44.520 --> 12:45.940
It's just training,
but don't let your guard down!

12:46.020 --> 12:47.650
I know!

12:53.820 --> 12:55.240
Here I go!

12:59.620 --> 13:00.910
All right!

13:03.120 --> 13:04.250
How's that?

13:04.330 --> 13:05.170
Did you see it?

13:05.250 --> 13:06.380
Did you see that?

13:06.460 --> 13:08.130
Well done, Cybil.

13:08.460 --> 13:11.300
That's our youngest,
number-one attacker for you!

13:11.590 --> 13:13.090
Nice strike.

13:13.340 --> 13:15.970
With me in the picture,
Silver Sword's as steady as a rock!

13:22.430 --> 13:24.440
Heal him while I defend!

13:24.520 --> 13:25.440
Got it!

13:42.710 --> 13:43.710
Lululi!

13:44.210 --> 13:45.670
Hurry up and heal him!

13:45.750 --> 13:47.040
Yes!

13:47.380 --> 13:48.920
(Healing Light)
Heal!

13:51.630 --> 13:53.720
Her judgment seems slower than usual?

13:54.590 --> 13:55.550
Damn it!

13:55.630 --> 13:56.930
You bastard!

13:57.010 --> 13:58.010
Cybil!

13:58.930 --> 14:00.350
I'll pull aggro again!

14:00.430 --> 14:01.600
You stay back!

14:03.390 --> 14:04.940
Get hit already! Damn it!

14:05.020 --> 14:06.940
Don't lose your temper! Step aside!

14:07.230 --> 14:08.060
No!

14:08.150 --> 14:09.690
I'll finish it myself!

14:11.280 --> 14:12.530
It won't come out.

14:24.870 --> 14:26.540
Cybil, run!

14:26.620 --> 14:29.750
You're in my way, filthy dog!

14:41.140 --> 14:42.180
What?

14:50.860 --> 14:53.230
The hologram generator broke?

14:54.570 --> 14:55.940
No way!

14:59.660 --> 15:01.240
Well...

15:01.330 --> 15:02.530
I have a question for you.

15:02.620 --> 15:04.370
Wait a minute!

15:05.120 --> 15:07.040
I have a question for you.

15:07.410 --> 15:08.250
Yes?

15:10.710 --> 15:13.300
- It's not like you're walking a dog, I...
- Damn it!

15:14.250 --> 15:16.800
He defeated a werewolf in one blow?

15:17.130 --> 15:19.840
And all I did was cut it,
but I was so smug about it.

15:19.930 --> 15:22.470
That person's special,
so don't take it to heart.

15:22.550 --> 15:24.260
That's right.

15:24.350 --> 15:26.230
You did a good job, Cybil.

15:26.310 --> 15:28.350
You'll be fine if you keep on fighting.

15:28.440 --> 15:29.480
No!

15:29.560 --> 15:31.860
I can't bear the name
of Silver Sword like this.

15:32.150 --> 15:36.530
I have to get stronger!

15:37.110 --> 15:40.280
We have to find an attacker again.

15:42.950 --> 15:45.740
The adventurers are already there?

15:45.830 --> 15:46.750
Already?

15:46.830 --> 15:48.750
You know something, don't you?

15:48.830 --> 15:51.750
I've been swarmed since this morning!

15:51.830 --> 15:53.420
I'm sorry, Miss.

15:53.500 --> 15:55.000
Let me explain.

15:55.500 --> 15:56.630
"In the secret quest,

15:56.710 --> 15:59.930
there's a relic
that grants you a Dia skill."

16:00.300 --> 16:03.430
This rumor started spreading
among the adventurers.

16:03.510 --> 16:04.680
Rumor?

16:04.760 --> 16:06.930
Why would anyone believe such a thing?

16:07.020 --> 16:11.150
There are many people who would do
anything to obtain Dia skills.

16:11.650 --> 16:12.600
So,

16:12.690 --> 16:15.520
what should we do
about the chaos at the counter?

16:15.730 --> 16:18.360
The Guild will make
an official announcement tomorrow

16:18.440 --> 16:20.150
that the secret quest was fabricated

16:20.240 --> 16:21.110
and won't allow it to go...

16:21.200 --> 16:22.530
Do you think adventurers
are rational enough

16:22.610 --> 16:26.240
to stop just because
of a Guild announcement?

16:27.120 --> 16:28.120
Anyway,

16:28.200 --> 16:30.960
we'll do our best to find the one
who spread the rumor.

16:31.040 --> 16:32.750
Until then, please bear with us.

16:34.500 --> 16:36.670
I think I understand the situation now.

16:36.750 --> 16:39.340
I'll go back and finish up today's work.

16:39.420 --> 16:42.180
If you find out anything else,
let me know right away.

16:42.260 --> 16:43.260
Okay.

16:53.650 --> 16:55.360
Sorry to keep you waiting, Lululi.

16:55.860 --> 16:57.820
Is Ms. Alina all right?

16:57.900 --> 17:00.570
She's really mad about the secret quest.

17:00.650 --> 17:02.240
We need to do something
as soon as possible.

17:02.490 --> 17:03.780
You're right.

17:03.860 --> 17:04.870
That's right.

17:05.240 --> 17:06.410
During the training just now,

17:06.490 --> 17:08.620
you seemed hesitant in your movements.

17:09.040 --> 17:10.330
Did something happen?

17:11.830 --> 17:13.080
Well,

17:13.540 --> 17:16.630
it must be because I've never teamed up
with a great sword user.

17:16.710 --> 17:18.630
So I'm not used to it.

17:19.380 --> 17:20.420
I see.

17:20.920 --> 17:22.130
But the main reason

17:22.220 --> 17:24.760
is that the staff probably
isn't right for you.

17:25.140 --> 17:26.430
You're right.

17:26.510 --> 17:29.770
After all, the staff you used
was destroyed by the dark god.

17:30.140 --> 17:31.930
That's why…

17:32.020 --> 17:32.850
Here.

17:32.940 --> 17:34.400
It's a gift from me and Leader.

17:37.310 --> 17:38.610
This is…

17:38.980 --> 17:42.780
It's crafted based on the staff
you used previously.

17:43.200 --> 17:45.530
It's better than this temporary staff.

17:46.700 --> 17:48.830
I thought I couldn't use it anymore.

17:48.910 --> 17:50.450
But why?

17:50.740 --> 17:53.040
Didn't you work tirelessly
to take care of us?

17:53.120 --> 17:54.870
If it weren't for you,

17:54.960 --> 17:57.040
we'd still be in bed.

17:57.130 --> 17:58.380
Not at all.

17:58.790 --> 18:01.960
I just did what I was supposed to do.

18:03.220 --> 18:04.510
I knew you'd think so.

18:04.590 --> 18:06.840
But what you think you're supposed to do

18:06.930 --> 18:08.970
is actually very special to us.

18:09.050 --> 18:11.100
Yes, yes, he's right.

18:14.980 --> 18:17.150
So, thank you.

18:21.150 --> 18:22.570
I should be the one

18:23.940 --> 18:25.530
thanking you.

18:33.540 --> 18:36.080
Ms. Alina, it's lunch break now.

18:36.170 --> 18:37.880
What are you doing?

18:37.960 --> 18:40.590
I want to take care
of some overtime work first.

18:41.340 --> 18:44.590
Why don't you reduce
the number of requests?

18:45.880 --> 18:49.220
Precisely because you handle requests
twice as fast as others,

18:49.300 --> 18:52.390
you also have twice
as much paperwork to handle.

18:52.470 --> 18:53.430
Just bear with it

18:53.520 --> 18:56.310
and flatter the adventurers
when they brag,

18:56.390 --> 18:58.850
you can then reduce
the number of requests, right?

18:58.940 --> 18:59.940
Let me tell you.

19:00.360 --> 19:02.360
Even if we take our time at the counter,

19:02.440 --> 19:04.780
someone has to process
those request forms.

19:04.860 --> 19:08.780
But it doesn't have to be you.

19:09.240 --> 19:10.240
However,

19:10.530 --> 19:13.040
I don't want to play dirty like that.

19:13.700 --> 19:15.040
In a workplace,

19:15.120 --> 19:18.000
people like you are the most useful
and easily worked to the bone.

19:18.960 --> 19:21.500
I think so too.

19:24.670 --> 19:25.630
Indeed.

19:26.050 --> 19:27.170
This rumor

19:27.260 --> 19:30.180
has a lot in common
with Rufus' words and actions.

19:30.260 --> 19:32.390
I don't think it's a coincidence.

19:33.220 --> 19:34.850
His goal

19:34.930 --> 19:37.180
was to obtain Dia skills.

19:37.690 --> 19:39.940
However, such a relic didn't exist.

19:40.230 --> 19:42.310
Instead, he revived the Dark God.

19:43.020 --> 19:44.110
In other words,

19:44.190 --> 19:46.400
the goal of the person
who spread the rumor...

19:46.780 --> 19:48.860
Was to revive the new Dark God?

19:48.950 --> 19:50.280
No way.

19:51.950 --> 19:55.450
The Dark God can only be revived
by devouring human souls.

19:55.830 --> 19:57.080
Only by deceiving adventurers

19:57.160 --> 19:58.960
and luring them to the hidden dungeon...

19:59.540 --> 20:01.670
Can they be sacrificed to the Dark God.

20:01.750 --> 20:03.750
That's the worst!

20:04.250 --> 20:06.090
Hey, wait a minute.

20:06.170 --> 20:08.300
Why are you all gathered here?

20:08.630 --> 20:10.050
I'm sorry.

20:10.130 --> 20:11.800
Stuff like secret quests and the dark god

20:11.890 --> 20:14.050
isn't something we can discuss
at the Guild headquarters.

20:14.140 --> 20:17.060
After all, we don't know
who might be eavesdropping.

20:17.140 --> 20:18.640
We have some good news too.

20:18.730 --> 20:20.560
According to the intel team,

20:20.640 --> 20:23.440
we've roughly figured out
where the rumor came from.

20:23.520 --> 20:24.860
Well then, let's get going.

20:24.940 --> 20:26.070
Let's go right now!

20:26.320 --> 20:27.780
No, wait.

20:27.860 --> 20:29.280
Once we come up with a plan,

20:29.360 --> 20:31.160
we'll let you know.

20:31.360 --> 20:33.240
I guess I have no choice.

20:33.320 --> 20:35.580
As long as I can attend
the Centennial Festival,

20:35.660 --> 20:38.250
I'm willing to do anything.

20:39.750 --> 20:41.330
Well, Ms. Alina.

20:41.710 --> 20:44.540
Isn't it too difficult to finish up
all these request forms on your own

20:44.630 --> 20:46.090
before the Centennial Festival?

20:46.170 --> 20:47.840
I have no choice but to do it, right?

20:48.380 --> 20:49.420
What if I told you

20:49.510 --> 20:52.470
there's a way for you
to handle all this work smoothly?

20:54.850 --> 20:59.520
Anyway, you're going to ask
for something weird in return, right?

20:59.600 --> 21:01.390
Well, that's...

21:01.810 --> 21:03.900
I just want to help you

21:03.980 --> 21:06.820
and go on a date with you
at the Centennial Festival.

21:07.110 --> 21:08.150
See?

21:08.230 --> 21:10.110
There's no way I'm agreeing to that!

21:10.190 --> 21:11.610
Then, two days...

21:11.700 --> 21:12.700
No, just one day.

21:12.780 --> 21:14.490
Just for one day, let's go on a date.

21:14.570 --> 21:17.450
No way! Over my dead body!

21:17.740 --> 21:19.240
But at this rate,

21:19.330 --> 21:22.290
you might not even make it
to the Centennial Festival.

21:24.920 --> 21:25.960
That's true.

21:26.040 --> 21:27.460
This current situation

21:27.540 --> 21:30.170
isn't something I can handle on my own.

21:30.670 --> 21:33.180
I can't have my cake and eat it too.

21:33.260 --> 21:34.550
It's only for one day.

21:34.640 --> 21:38.010
As long as I sacrifice one day
to be with this insufferable guy,

21:38.100 --> 21:40.220
I can be happy for the other two days.

21:40.600 --> 21:41.430
Even if that one day

21:41.520 --> 21:43.230
makes me so disgusted
that I want to puke blood,

21:43.310 --> 21:45.940
that memory can be overwritten
by the next two days!

21:46.770 --> 21:48.940
You said your inner thoughts out loud.

21:49.020 --> 21:50.940
Do you hate it that much?

21:51.030 --> 21:53.280
I'll agree to it.

21:53.650 --> 21:54.780
Really?

21:54.860 --> 21:56.910
I have no choice but to agree.

21:57.200 --> 21:58.780
Don't get the wrong idea.

21:59.830 --> 22:00.830
Let's do our best.

22:01.080 --> 22:03.790
I'll definitely go
to the Centennial Festival this year!

22:04.120 --> 22:05.750
Whether it's overtime
or that rumor-mongering jerk,

22:05.830 --> 22:07.040
I'll beat them all up!

22:07.130 --> 22:08.290
Leave it to me.

22:08.380 --> 22:10.840
Let's eliminate overtime
and go to the Centennial Festival,

22:11.630 --> 22:12.880
Ms. Alina!

22:17.830 --> 22:22.060
(6 Days Before the Centennial Festival)

23:53.440 --> 23:54.270
Next episode.

23:54.360 --> 23:56.320
I may be the Silver Sword's rear attacker,

23:56.400 --> 23:58.820
but I'll catch the rumor-mongering jerk.

23:58.820 --> 24:00.820
(Next Episode: I May Be the Silver Sword's Rear
Attacker, But I'll Catch the Rumor-mongering Jerk)
